# Mobile project (Expo + React Native)

Expert defaults: Expo SDK 55, React Native 0.83, React 19, TypeScript strict, Apollo Client + GraphQL, MobX + mobx-react-lite, React Navigation v7, i18next, Expo Notifications / Auth Session / Location / Image Picker.

## Separation of concerns

| Area | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `screens/` | Page UI + orchestration |
| `components/` | Reusable presentational UI |
| `stores/` | MobX state |
| `services/` | API + platform integrations |
| `hooks/` | Reusable logic |
| `navigation/` | Routing |
| `theme/` | Design tokens |
| `types/` | Shared TS types |
| `utils/` | Pure helpers |
| `constants/` | App constants |
| `i18n/` | Localization |
| `config/` | Env + runtime config |
| `contexts/` | React context |

## Typing & file size

- TypeScript strict; avoid `any` unless unavoidable.
- Prefer `type` for unions, `interface` for extensible objects; export shared types from `types/`.
- Target: components under ~200 lines, screens under ~300 lines; extract hooks, stores, or services when logic grows.

## Naming

- Files: `UserCard.tsx`, `ProfileScreen.tsx`, `useAuth.ts`, `AuthStore.ts`, `AuthService.ts`, `formatPhone.ts`, `storageKeys.ts`, `auth.ts` (types).
- Symbols: PascalCase components/enums, `use*` hooks, camelCase functions, `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for immutable exported constants.

## Imports (order)

1. React → 2. React Native → 3. Third-party → 4. Navigation → 5. Services → 6. Stores → 7. Hooks → 8. Components → 9. Theme → 10. Types → 11. Utils → 12. Relative.

Prefer path aliases: `@/components`, `@/screens`, `@/services`, `@/stores`, `@/hooks`, `@/theme`, `@/types`, `@/utils`, `@/constants`, `@/config`, `@/navigation`.

## Folder layout (reference)

```text
src/
  components/   (common/, forms/, feedback/, layout/, feature-name/)
  config/       env.ts, apollo.ts
  constants/    routes.ts, storageKeys.ts
  contexts/     e.g. RootStoreContext.ts
  hooks/
  i18n/         index.ts, locales/en.json, fr.json
  navigation/   AppNavigator.tsx, types.ts, …
  screens/      FeatureScreen.tsx, optional FeatureView.tsx
  services/     api/, auth/, storage/, notifications/, location/, …
  stores/       RootStore.ts, feature stores
  theme/        colors, spacing, typography, index
  types/
  utils/
App.tsx
```

## Components (`components/`)

- Reusable, props-driven; no direct store access; no API calls.
- `StyleSheet.create`; theme tokens only; avoid raw hex/spacing/font strings unless dynamic and trivial.

## Screens (`screens/`)

- Navigation, store/hook wiring, props for child components; keep heavy logic out (use hooks / stores).
- If large: extract `*View.tsx` + orchestration hook.

## Hooks (`hooks/`)

- Reusable logic; may use stores/services; no UI rendering.

## MobX

- Stores: observables, computed, actions, async; no UI, no React imports.
- Root store composes feature stores; `makeAutoObservable(this, {}, { autoBind: true })`.
- Persist via `StorageService`, not raw AsyncStorage.

## Apollo / GraphQL

- Calls from `services/api/`, hooks, or stores—not raw operations embedded in screens.
- Organize `queries/`, `mutations/`, `ApolloClientService.ts`; use codegen types when available; normalize errors for UX.

## Services

- Wrap Auth, Storage, Notifications, Location, Image Picker, Updates, etc.; typed results, meaningful errors, no UI.

## Navigation

- Param lists in `navigation/types.ts`; type `useNavigation` / route props.

## Theme

- Tokens in `theme/` (colors, spacing, typography, radii, shadows)—no magic literals in UI.

## i18n

- All user-visible strings via `useTranslation` / `t('namespace.key')`; namespaced keys (`auth.login`, `errors.network`).

## Errors & security

- Catch at service/store boundaries; user-facing copy via `t()`; centralize logging.
- No secrets in source; validate external input; sanitize URLs/files; secure token storage when required.

## AsyncStorage

- Only through `StorageService` (`getString`, `getObject<T>`, `setObject`, `remove`).

## Utils & constants

- Utils: pure, side-effect-free, testable.
- Constants: routes, storage keys, timeouts, pagination defaults (`as const` objects).

## Config

- URLs, flags, build metadata in `config/`—no hardcoded secrets or env-specific URLs in random files.

## Performance

- `observer` on stateful screens; `React.memo` / `useCallback` / `useMemo` when justified; `FlatList` for long lists; avoid redundant observable reads.

## Testing priority

- Utilities, services, stores, custom hooks first; UI tests secondary.

## When generating code

1. Match folder roles above. 2. Small focused files. 3. Strict types. 4. Theme tokens. 5. Translation keys. 6. Typed navigation. 7. Logic in stores/hooks/services. 8. No duplication. 9. No magic strings/numbers in UI. 10. Error handling at boundaries. 11. Path aliases. 12. Respect existing patterns in the repo.

## Screen pattern

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { observer } from 'mobx-react-lite';
import { HomeView } from './HomeView';
import { useHomeScreen } from '@/hooks/useHomeScreen';

export const HomeScreen = observer(() => {
  const props = useHomeScreen();
  return <HomeView {...props} />;
});
```

## Store pattern

```ts
import { makeAutoObservable } from 'mobx';

export class AuthStore {
  token: string | null = null;
  isLoading = false;

  constructor() {
    makeAutoObservable(this, {}, { autoBind: true });
  }

  get isAuthenticated() {
    return !!this.token;
  }

  async login(email: string, password: string) {
    this.isLoading = true;
    try {
      // AuthService
    } finally {
      this.isLoading = false;
    }
  }
}
```

## Anti-patterns

- API calls inside dumb components; AsyncStorage outside `StorageService`; hardcoded copy/colors; unjustified `any`; huge monolith files; duplicated domain logic; inline-only navigation types; mixing UI and domain; reusable components reaching into stores.

## New feature workflow

1. Domain types → 2. GraphQL ops → 3. Services → 4. Stores → 5. Hooks → 6. Components → 7. Screen + view → 8. Translations → 9. Routes → 10. Tests.

## Architecture map

| Concern | Where |
|---------|--------|
| API | `services/api/` |
| OAuth | `services/auth/` |
| Notifications | `services/notifications/` |
| Persistence | `services/storage/` |
| Business state | `stores/` |
| Reusable logic | `hooks/` |
| Widgets | `components/` |
| Pages | `screens/` |
| Routes | `navigation/` |
| Types | `types/` |
| Helpers | `utils/` |
| Tokens | `theme/` |
| Copy | `i18n/` |

Style: feature-oriented subfolders where helpful; MVVM-ish—screen = controller, view = presentation, store/hook = view model, service = infrastructure.

## Summary

Strict TypeScript, clear layers, reusable UI, service-backed integrations, MobX state, Apollo for GraphQL, typed navigation, themed styles, full i18n, low duplication, production maintainability.
